(no outgoing edges to Specification - rejected option, retained as Foundation knowledge); would strain → VT-02.

= Technology Option - Pepper on the walk (rejected) [TECH-07] =

**Report Format:** §1.3 Technology

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|TECH-07
|Name|Pepper on the walk (rejected)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Vendor documentation: Pepper is designed for indoor use.
|Category|Social Robot
|Capabilities|A robot companion outdoors: presence, voice, tablet.
|Limitations|Flat indoor floors only; rain; kerbs and gravel; battery; speed set by the robot, not the resident.
|Maturity and feasibility|Not feasible outdoors.
|Failure and fallback behaviour|Not applicable - rejected.
|Benefits|Strong social presence on the walk.
|Drawbacks|Terrain and weather rule it out.
|Selected or rejected|Rejected. Indoor corridor walks beside Pepper on rain days: possible, not specified this cycle.

