= Technology Option - Stress wristband (rejected) [TECH-09] =

**Report Format:** §1.3 Technology

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|TECH-09
|Name|Stress wristband (rejected)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Group reasoning. Consumer wristbands estimate heart rate and skin conductance.
|Category|Wearable / Sensing
|Capabilities|Could sense stress and pace the practice to it.
|Limitations|Accuracy in older adults uncertain; worn all day; skin irritation; taken off.
|Maturity and feasibility|Medium.
|Failure and fallback behaviour|Not applicable - rejected.
|Benefits|Could detect distress the guide cannot see.
|Drawbacks|Continuous body data; monitoring felt as surveillance (HFC-07); violates HV-03.
|Selected or rejected|Rejected. Distress is left to people: the companion and the care worker.

== Graph edges ==

(no outgoing edges to Specification - rejected option, retained as Foundation knowledge).

